entries.english:
Johann Philipp [von Greiffenclau], Bischof zu Würzburg, enfeoffs the brothers and sons of Anton Philibert von Rosenbach—Lothar Josef Heinrich, Domherr zu Mainz und Würzburg; Johann Philipp, Domherr zu Bamberg und Würzburg; Karl Ignaz Adolf, Domherr zu Bamberg; Franz Philipp Ludwig, bischöflicher Rat; and Adalbert Friedrich von Rosenbach—for themselves, and Lothar Josef Heinrich as guardian for his minor brother Karl Christoph, with the following fiefs of the male line:
- Thundorf Castle, with all rights, appurtenances, and revenues, except only the farmstead;
- the deserted settlement of Ransbach, with its mill and farmstead and all rights and revenues;
- the villages of Theinfeld and Rothhausen, with all rights, holdings, and revenues there;
- a holding in Maßbach behind the churchyard;
- the holdings in Poppenlauer;
- the holdings in Ebertshausen;
- half the tithe at Altenmünster;
- one third of the tithe at Oberlauringen;
- one eighth of the tithe at Alsleben;
- one quarter of the tithe at Ober- and Untereßfeld;
- a vineyard and two wooded tracts at Thundorf.
The bishop further enfeoffs them with the following properties, which Veit Ulrich von Schaumberg had held as allodial property and then conveyed to the Würzburg bishopric as fiefs:
- the farmstead and vineyards at Thundorf;
- the lake at Weißensee;
- a fishery in the Lauer below Maßbach;
- a fishery in the Lauer within the Rothhausen district;
- three quarters of the mill at Rothhausen;
- two holdings at Theinfeld;
- two freehold holdings at Weichtungen;
- four rent-bearing fiefs at Stadtlauringen;
- nine holdings and eleven fiefs in Maßbach;
- the Brandmühle below Maßbach;
- five holdings and four fiefs in Poppenlauer;
- three holdings and one fief in Nüdlingen;
- one fief at Rannungen;
- a field holding at Hesselbach;
- the Herlingsberg wood;
- the male-line fief at Prappach.
They had purchased these properties from the brothers Georg Dietrich, Wilhelm Ludwig, Wilhelm Ulrich, Georg Wilhelm, Johann Sigmund, Johann Philipp, and Johann Wilhelm von Schaumberg.
Finally, the bishop also enfeoffs them with the following properties, originally held as fiefs from the County of Henneberg and then the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar, which passed to Würzburg as a result of an agreement between the Würzburg bishopric and the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar:
- the Zent court at Maßbach, subsequently moved to Poppenlauer, with all appurtenances and rights, excluding the villages of Maßbach and Volkershausen;
- half the Vogtei at Poppenlauer;
- two holdings in Maßbach and a meadow between Maßbach and Rothhausen;
- one quarter of the tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third of a small quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third and one quarter of a full quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- four wooded tracts near Maßbach;
- the wine rents and rent revenues at Schonungen. If the von Rosenbach family should ever have no male heirs, the Würzburg bishopric is obliged to pay the family's female heirs 2,000 Reichstaler for these revenues.
Their father Anton Philibert von Rosenbach's share in these fiefs passed to them after his death. Their uncles Philipp Ludwig and Franz Albrecht von Rosenbach still hold shares in them.
Sealed by the bishop with his privy seal. Endorsements: abstract (18th century).
